pped amount was about 0.09979 ETH rather than a full 0.1 ETH. The bridge fee took part of it, and 0.00004 ETH was kept on base1 for swap gas and the reserve.\n\nNo legs are in transit.","outcome":{"kind":"target_reached"},"balances":{"eth1":{"ETH":"49700000000000000","USDC":"0"},"base1":{"ETH":"20000000000000","USDC":"299079999"}},"in_transit_legs":[]},"id":"toolu_01KSqizp16FuQGDrmqcs89G6"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":39,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"reported\":true}","toolCallId":"toolu_01KSqizp16FuQGDrmqcs89G6","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_report_result","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":40,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your 0.1 ETH from the Ethereum wallet (`eth1`) is now 299.079999 USDC on the Base wallet (`base1`).\n\nI bridged the ETH to Base first, then swapped it to USDC there. Both transactions confirmed, and I checked the `base1` ETH balance after the bridge, before the swap. The quoted cost was $1.76, within your $8 cap. I didn't read back an actual cost, only the balances.\n\n| Wallet | ETH | USDC |\n|---|---|---|\n| `eth1` | 0.0497 | 0 |\n| `base1` | 0.00002 | 299.079999 |\n\nAbout 0.09979 ETH was swapped, not the full 0.1. The bridge fee took part of it, and I left 0.00004 ETH on `base1` to cover the swap's gas and keep the required reserve for one more transaction. Both wallets still have enough ETH for that."}]}],"completeness":{"transcriptCaptureComplete":true,"modelObservedTruncation":false,"auxiliarySourceComplete":true,"finalAnswerPresent":true,"nativeVisibleEvidenceAvailable":true},"gaps":[],"publication":{"kind":"public_redacted","sourceConversationSha256":"81f11437d4963ed8dc598a772772d340d97a9e44c2017331671ef9dd5b8b1078","redactions":{}}}}
